          "text": "# SV-MATH-001 \u2014 ALLOW Gate Admissibility\n\n## 1. Assumptions and bounded claim\n\nBecause no authoritative GCAT/BCAT specification, implementation, or existing Lean definitions were supplied, the proof uses the following explicit model:\n\n1. A proposed rewrite has a geometric source and destination and an ontological source and destination.\n2. **Geometric boundary preservation** means that the source lies on the distinguished boundary exactly when the destination does.\n3. **Bounded divergence** means that the engine\u2019s divergence measure between source and destination is at most the configured limit.\n4. **Ontological consistency** means that the engine\u2019s compatibility relation holds between the source and destination ontology values.\n5. The only ALLOW inference rule requires all three conditions.\n6. The executable ALLOW gate is the Boolean conjunction of decidable checks for those conditions.\n\nUnder these assumptions, geometric boundary preservation, bounded divergence, and ontological consistency are jointly necessary and sufficient\u2014and therefore jointly complete\u2014for ALLOW admissibility.\n\nThis is a claim about the formal model below. It does not by itself establish correspondence with an external GCAT/BCAT implementation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Lean 4 formalization\n\n```lean\nimport Std\n\nnamespace SVMATH001\n\nuniverse uG uO\n\n/-- Abstract GCAT/BCAT engine data. -/\nstructure Engine (G : Type uG) (O : Type uO) where\n  /-- Distinguished geometric boundary predicate. -/\n  boundary : G \u2192 Prop\n\n  /-- Divergence or displacement assigned to a geometric rewrite. -/\n  divergence : G \u2192 G \u2192 Nat\n\n  /-- Maximum divergence accepted by the ALLOW gate. -/\n  divergenceLimit : Nat\n\n  /-- Ontological compatibility relation. -/\n  compatible : O \u2192 O \u2192 Prop\n\n  /-- Executability assumptions for the Boolean gate. -/\n  boundaryDecidable :\n    (x : G) \u2192 Decidable (boundary x)\n\n  compatibleDecidable :\n    (a b : O) \u2192 Decidable (compatible a b)\n\n\n/-- A proposed GCAT/BCAT rewrite. -/\nstructure Candidate (G : Type uG) (O : Type uO) where\n  sourceGeometry : G\n  targetGeometry : G\n  sourceOntology : O\n  targetOntology : O\n\n\nsection Semantics\n\nvariable {G : Type uG} {O : Type uO}\n\n/--\nGeometric boundary preservation.\n\nThe rewrite neither creates nor destroys membership in the distinguished\ngeometric boundary.\n-/\ndef GeometricBoundaryPreserving\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O) : Prop :=\n  E.boundary c.sourceGeometry \u2194 E.boundary c.targetGeometry\n\n\n/--\nBounded divergence.\n\nThe geometric displacement of the candidate is within the engine's\nconfigured divergence limit.\n-/\ndef BoundedDivergence\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O) : Prop :=\n  E.divergence c.sourceGeometry c.targetGeometry \u2264 E.divergenceLimit\n\n\n/--\nOntological consistency.\n\nThe source ontology may consistently rewrite to the target ontology.\n-/\ndef OntologicallyConsistent\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O) : Prop :=\n  E.compatible c.sourceOntology c.targetOntology\n\n\n/--\nThe ALLOW admissibility judgment.\n\nThere is exactly one introduction rule. It requires geometric boundary\npreservation, bounded divergence, and ontological consistency.\n-/\ninductive Admissible\n    (E : Engine G O) : Candidate G O \u2192 Prop where\n  | allow {c : Candidate G O} :\n      GeometricBoundaryPreserving E c \u2192\n      BoundedDivergence E c \u2192\n      OntologicallyConsistent E c \u2192\n      Admissible E c\n\n\n/--\nNecessary-and-sufficient characterization of semantic admissibility.\n-/\ntheorem admissible_iff_three_conditions\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O) :\n    Admissible E c \u2194\n      GeometricBoundaryPreserving E c \u2227\n      BoundedDivergence E c \u2227\n      OntologicallyConsistent E c := by\n  constructor\n  \u00b7 intro h\n    cases h with\n    | allow hBoundary hDivergence hOntology =>\n        exact \u27e8hBoundary, hDivergence, hOntology\u27e9\n  \u00b7 rintro \u27e8hBoundary, hDivergence, hOntology\u27e9\n    exact Admissible.allow hBoundary hDivergence hOntology\n\n\n/-- Boundary preservation is necessary for admissibility. -/\ntheorem boundary_preservation_necessary\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O)\n    (h : Admissible E c) :\n    GeometricBoundaryPreserving E c :=\n  (admissible_iff_three_conditions E c).mp h |>.1\n\n\n/-- Bounded divergence is necessary for admissibility. -/\ntheorem bounded_divergence_necessary\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O)\n    (h : Admissible E c) :\n    BoundedDivergence E c :=\n  (admissible_iff_three_conditions E c).mp h |>.2.1\n\n\n/-- Ontological consistency is necessary for admissibility. -/\ntheorem ontological_consistency_necessary\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O)\n    (h : Admissible E c) :\n    OntologicallyConsistent E c :=\n  (admissible_iff_three_conditions E c).mp h |>.2.2\n\n\n/-- The three conditions are jointly sufficient for admissibility. -/\ntheorem three_conditions_sufficient\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O)\n    (hBoundary : GeometricBoundaryPreserving E c)\n    (hDivergence : BoundedDivergence E c)\n    (hOntology : OntologicallyConsistent E c) :\n    Admissible E c :=\n  Admissible.allow hBoundary hDivergence hOntology\n\nend Semantics\n\n\nsection ExecutableGate\n\nvariable {G : Type uG} {O : Type uO}\n\n/-- Executable geometric-boundary check. -/\ndef boundaryCheck\n    (E : Engine G O)\n    (c : Candidate G O) : Bool := by\n  letI : Decidable (E.boundary c.sourceGeometry) :=\n    E.boundaryDecidable c.sourceGeometry\n  letI : Decidable (E.boundary c.targetGeometry) :=\n    E.boundaryDecidable c.targetGeometry\n  exact decide (GeometricBoundaryPreserving E"
